# Project 2 - Seven Segment Display

## Objective

Learn to light up 0-9 on a Seven Segment Display, controlled via button on breadboard.

## Key Hardware

- Raspberry Pi 5 (8 GB)
- Seven Segment Display
- CanaKit Starter Kit
- Wired keyboard and mouse
- Monitor
- Bread board and electronics starter kit

## Software

- Raspberry Pi OS
- Python 3 / Thonny

## Goals

- Light up display and learn pin layout
- Control display with button press
- Create and run program to have display light up numbers 0-9 sequentially
- Continue learning breadboard and programming basics

## Status

Completed.

## Challenges

This project was similar in essence to lighting up an individual LED. By using multiple GPIO pins, I was able to easily - yet tediously - light up the Seven Segment Display in the pattern I desired. 
My next goal is to use a chip to limit the GPIO's needed to control the display.
